<https://n2t.net/ark:/27023/29b1586a63b0c5cf884207def4e2c647> <https://colonialcollections.nl/schema#inscription> "inscription: ‘H.M.S. BOADICEA,<BR />16 GUNS IRON S, CORVETTE 4140 TONS<BR />UNDER REPAIR IN THE<BR />GRAVING DOCK, TABLE BAY,<BR />CAPE OF GOOD HOPE.<BR />DIMENSIONS OF THE DOCK.<BR />Length on floor 500 feet<BR />Width of Entrance 68 feet<BR />Depth over Cill 26 feet - at high water of Spring tides<BR />Do. 21 feet - at low water of Spring tides<BR /><BR />The graving Dock forms a part of the Docks & extensive Harbour Improvements now being carried out in Table Bay from designs by and under the Directions of Sir John Cood, C.E.’" .
